WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:03.268
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.268 --> 00:00:05.670
- [Narrator] Seven miles
off Estonia's west coast

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.246
in eastern Europe lies
the small island of Kihnu,

00:00:09.246 --> 00:00:13.348
a bucolic and serene place
that feels lost in time.

00:00:13.348 --> 00:00:16.149
Home to just 400 people,
it functions like one

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.078
of the world's few matriarchal societies.

00:00:19.078 --> 00:00:23.782
This is a place where women
rule, well, mostly everything.

00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:26.532
Hello, welcome to Kihnu Island.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.447
- [Narrator] One such
tradition is that Kihnu's men

00:00:50.447 --> 00:00:53.677
spend months away at sea
fishing for the island.

00:00:53.677 --> 00:00:55.950
Meanwhile, Kihnu's women
are in charge of leading

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.700
the community and
preserving its way of life.

00:01:15.631 --> 00:01:19.798
She is making skirts because
she has five granddaughters.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.686
- [Narrator] The clothes,
the music, the dancing,

00:02:04.686 --> 00:02:06.800
all of it has been recognized by UNESCO

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.217
on its Intangible Cultural Heritage list.

00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:21.867
- [Narrator] The same list
acknowledges Kihnu's women

00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:25.700
as the custodians of
their island's heritage.

